### 4.3 Estimation of the number of polarized \(\Lambda\) hyperons

For the yield of \(\Lambda+\bar{\Lambda}\), \(dN/dy=16.7+12.7=29.4\), which is already corrected for \(\Xi\), \(\Xi^{0}\), and \(\Omega\) feed-down (15% contribution altogether, \(\Xi^{-}\to\Lambda\pi^{-}\) with branching ratio 99.9%, \(\Xi^{0}\to\Lambda\pi^{0}\) with branching ration 99.5%, \(\Omega^{-}\to\Lambda K^{-}\), \(\Xi^{0}\pi^{-}\) or \(\Xi^{-}\pi^{0}\) with branching ratio 100%), but includes \(\Sigma\) feed-down (\(\Sigma^{0}\to\Lambda\gamma\), branching ratio 100%). To calculate the primordial \(\Lambda\) yield, we need to know the \(\Sigma/\Lambda\) ratio.

According to the statistical model in the Boltzmann approximation, the particle density is given by Eq. (2.8), or

\[n\equiv\frac{N}{V}=\frac{g}{2\pi^{2}}m^{2}T\gamma_{S}^{|n_{s}|}\exp\left( \frac{n_{q}\mu_{q}}{T}\right)\exp\left(\frac{n_{s}\mu_{s}}{T}\right)K_{2}\left( \frac{m}{T}\right),\]

