The large orbital angular momentum created in noncentral Au+Au collisions may lead to global quark polarization due to spin-orbital coupling. The global polarization of the produced quarks may result in a global \(\Lambda\) polarization [99]. Ref. [114] measured the \(\Lambda\) polarization directly and found out the \(P_{\Lambda}=(-23.3\pm 11.2)\times 10^{-2}\) for

